<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG Metals in Thailand joint venture.</title>
<headline>LG Metals in Thailand joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's largest gold producer LG Metals Corp, a unit of LG Group, said on Monday it had established a joint venture with Pranda Jewelry Co Ltd of Thailand to make and sell coins in precious metals.</p>
<p>A company spokesman said the joint venture, named LG-Pranda Co, will make coins and medals in Thailand with gold and silver produced by LG Metals.</p>
<p>The spokesman said LG Metals expected turnover to reach $50 million in 1997 and $100 million by 2000.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
